<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
	Appearance of the drop list window, opened by shift clicking a monster or a raid boss.

	Everything the player sees is defined here - every single string included, so no player facing
	text is left in the Java. The behavior (whether the window exists at all, which skill unlocks
	it, how many rows a page holds, whether the spoil groups are shown, and whether the server rates
	and the deep blue penalty are folded into the chances) lives server side, on
	config/mods/droplist.properties.

	The window is one single list, without any tab : each drop category of the monster shows up as
	a group - a header row holding its caption and the chance the whole group rolls, followed by its
	items sorted by decreasing chance. The groups are sorted by decreasing chance too, but the spoil
	ones land after the regular drops and the herb ones last.

	A group header is framed by the "separator" hairline, and it is only ever captioned "drop" or
	"spoil" - whether an item is looted or spoiled is the one thing the items sitting right under the
	header can't tell a player - followed by the rank of the group among the ones sharing that
	caption : "Дроп #1, Дроп #2, Спойл #1". The currency and the herb groups are looted just like the
	regular ones, so they carry the "drop" caption too.

	The name and the level of the monster land on the title bar of the dialog, generated by the HTM
	as "%npcName% - Ур.%npcLevel%".

	The first page opens on a header telling what the kill itself is worth, which the list of the
	drops can't tell : the amount of HP which has to be dealt to kill the monster, and the experience
	and the SP the very player reading the window earns for it. All three carry the champion bonuses
	of the monster - a champion doesn't own a bigger HP pool, it takes reduced damages, and the header
	shows the HP that reduction amounts to. The header takes the room of the item rows it covers, so
	the first page simply shows fewer drops and every page keeps the same height. It is dropped
	altogether by "DropListShowHeader" of config/mods/droplist.properties.

	A row draws the item icon on the left, then the item name on one line and the dropped amount
	right under it, the chance staying on the right - an adena amount is way too long to sit next
	to a name on a single line.

	The item icons come from data/xml/itemIcons.xml.

	<layout>
		Sizes of the generated tables. The group headers and the list rows are generated out of the
		very same width, which is what keeps them aligned - never describe a header on the HTM.

		width       : width, in pixels, of every generated table (group headers, rows, page
		              selector). Fed to the HTM as %width%. Keep it below 290, so the scrollbar
		              doesn't eat the last column.
		rowHeight   : height, in pixels, of a single row of the list. It has to leave room for the
		              icon and for the two stacked lines of text, so keep it above iconSize.
		groupHeight : height, in pixels, of a group header row. The page selector row uses it too.
		iconSize    : size, in pixels, the item icons are drawn at.
		pageWidth   : width, in pixels, of a single cell of the page selector - a page link or an
		              arrow. It is what keeps the selector on a single line : the amount of shown
		              links is whatever fits "width" out of that, so a cell is never squeezed under
		              the width its own content needs. Raise it if a selector ever wraps.
		maxPages    : maximum amount of page links shown by the page selector, centered on the
		              current page. It only ever lowers the amount "pageWidth" already allows, so
		              setting it high simply lets the width decide.
		nameChars   : amount of characters above which an item name is shortened, on the last word
		              boundary when possible. 0 never shortens - and lets a long name wrap, which
		              makes its row taller than the others. Roughly nameWidth / 6.
		ellipsis    : suffix appended to a shortened item name.
		separator   : client texture of the hairline drawn above and below every group header, which
		              is what cuts the list into groups. It is always drawn 1 pixel tall - the height
		              a page is padded up to counts on that. An empty value drops the frame.
		headerHeight     : height, in pixels, of a single line of the header of the first page. The
		                   header holds three of them - HP, experience and SP - plus the hairline
		                   closing it, and it costs the first page as many item rows as that height
		                   takes, rounded up. Raising it past a couple of row heights leaves little
		                   room for the drops themselves.
		headerLabelWidth : width, in pixels, of the caption column of the header. The value column
		                   takes whatever is left of "width", and the numbers are written with their
		                   thousand separators, so leave it room.
		overhead    : height, in pixels, everything but the group headers and the list rows takes on
		              the HTM - separators and the page selector row. Substracted from pageHeight to
		              know how much the page has to be padded with. Only worth touching after
		              editing the HTM. Rough guide : <br> 16, <br1> 8, a separator img 1, a selector
		              row 18.
		pageHeight  : total height, in pixels, every page is padded up to - the "overhead", the
		              group headers and the list rows included. Since it is the very same on every
		              page, the page selector always lands on the same spot ; and since it is set
		              slightly above the height of the dialog, the scrollbar stays shown
		              everywhere. 0 disables the padding. A page is
		              overhead + groups * (groupHeight + 2) + rows * rowHeight tall.

		iconWidth / nameWidth / chanceWidth : widths, in pixels, of the three columns. They must sum
		up to the layout width, otherwise the rows won't be aligned. The name column holds both the
		item name and, under it, the dropped amount.

	<colors>
		Every color of the dialog. An empty value keeps the client default : a transparent
		background for a row, a plain white text for a label.

		row / altRow       : background of the odd / even bands of a page. A group header is a band
		                     like any other, so the first header of a page takes "row", the item
		                     sitting right under it "altRow", and so on down the page.
		groupText          : caption of a group header row.
		headerText         : captions of the header of the first page.
		headerValue        : values of the header of the first page.
		name               : item names.
		count              : dropped amounts.
		highChance         : chance at or above "highChanceFrom".
		mediumChance       : chance at or above "mediumChanceFrom".
		lowChance          : anything below.
		disabled           : the label shown instead of an empty list.
		page / activePage  : page links / the current page.

		highChanceFrom / mediumChanceFrom : the two thresholds, in percent. They color the chance of
		                                    a group header as well as the one of a row.

	<labels>
		drop / spoil        : the only two captions a group header can carry. The spoil groups get the
		                      second one, every other group - drop, currency and herb alike - the
		                      first one.
		hp / exp / sp       : captions of the three lines of the header of the first page - the HP
		                      which has to be dealt to kill the monster, and the experience and the
		                      SP the kill is worth to the player reading the window.
		numberPrefix        : sits between a caption and the rank of the group among the ones sharing
		                      it, " #" giving "Дроп #1, Дроп #2, Спойл #1". The leading space belongs
		                      to the attribute, so any separator can be used.
		countPrefix         : put in front of a dropped amount, which tells it apart from the item
		                      name sitting right above it.
		countRange          : sits between the two bounds of an amount which isn't a fixed one.
		chancePattern       : DecimalFormat pattern a chance is rendered with, its amount of decimals
		                      included. "#0.##" gives "8.25", "#0.#" gives "8.3", "#0" gives "8".
		chanceSuffix        : appended to a rendered chance.
		nearZero            : shown instead of a chance the pattern would round down to a bare zero,
		                      which would read as "never". Holds its own suffix, and is worth
		                      rewriting along with "chancePattern" - "&lt;0.01%" only matches a
		                      pattern holding two decimals.

		A label needing a "&lt;" or a "&gt;" writes it as an XML entity, the way "nearZero" and the
		page arrows do. The window escapes them back on its way to the client, so a bare angle
		bracket would be swallowed as the start of a tag and take the rest of its cell with it.
		empty               : shown instead of an empty list.
		prevPage / nextPage : labels of the page selector arrows. Both live in a "pageWidth" wide
		                      cell, so keep them short.
-->
<list>
	<layout width="280" rowHeight="36" groupHeight="18" iconSize="32" pageWidth="26" maxPages="10" nameChars="30" ellipsis="..." separator="L2UI.SquareGray" overhead="43" pageHeight="440" headerHeight="16" headerLabelWidth="90" iconWidth="36" nameWidth="190" chanceWidth="54" />

	<colors row="000000" altRow="" groupText="LEVEL" headerText="LEVEL" headerValue="" name="" count="B09878" highChance="90EE90" mediumChance="BDB76B" lowChance="F08080" disabled="707070" page="" activePage="LEVEL" highChanceFrom="80" mediumChanceFrom="5" />

	<labels drop="Дроп" spoil="Спойл" hp="Здоровье" exp="Опыт" sp="SP" numberPrefix=" #" countPrefix="x" countRange="-" chancePattern="#0.##" chanceSuffix="%" nearZero="&lt;0.01%" empty="Здесь ничего не выпадает" prevPage="&lt;&lt;" nextPage="&gt;&gt;" />
</list>
